{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Graphing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Graphing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> of real numbers satisfy the following system of equations? \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b48951615b765a3c1135ff6029f1314427523f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^2+3y&amp;=9 \\\\ (|x|+|y|-4)^2 &amp;= 1 \\end{align*}\" width=\"146\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/648f5500bdc9679138a4406788a4208762d23caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Graphing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Graphing)\">Solution 1 (Graphing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Graphing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The second equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01cfac88414f5164fda3fbfef3cf7bc1cbfaeec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(|x|+|y| - 4)^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" />. We know that the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66585a4355d08551457edf35cc36e1e8c4a5599.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + |y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is a very simple diamond shape, so let's see if we can reduce this equation to that form: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4eae12e93fc1db2f8b8038aebdd206a7a6b5c323.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(|x|+|y| - 4)^2 = 1 \\implies |x|+|y| - 4 = \\pm 1 \\implies |x|+|y| = \\{3,5\\}.\\]\" width=\"481\" height=\"20\" />\nWe now have two separate graphs for this equation and one graph for the first equation, so let's put it on the coordinate plane:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/b/51bfd5ebea99685462e153dbecd9a825da8b2056.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  Label f;  f.p=fontsize(6);  xaxis(-8,8,Ticks(f, 1.0,0.5));  yaxis(-8,8,Ticks(f, 1.0,0.5));  real f(real x)  {  return 3-x;  }  draw(graph(f,0,3));  real f(real x)  {  return 3+x;  }  draw(graph(f,0,-3)); real f(real x)  {  return x-3;  }  draw(graph(f,0,3)); real f(real x)  {  return -x-3;  }  draw(graph(f,0,-3)); real f(real x)  {  return 5-x;  }  draw(graph(f,0,5));  real f(real x)  {  return 5+x;  }  draw(graph(f,0,-5)); real f(real x)  {  return x-5;  }  draw(graph(f,0,5)); real f(real x)  {  return -x-5;  }  draw(graph(f,0,-5));  real f(real x)  {  return 3-x;  }  draw(graph(f,0,3));  real f(real x)  {  return 3+x;  }  draw(graph(f,0,-3)); real f(real x)  {  return x-3;  }  draw(graph(f,0,3)); real f(real x)  {  return (-x^2)/3+3;  }  draw(graph(f,-5,5)); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"668\" />\nWe see from the graph that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> intersections, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c4efc7de2b7c8d6f24ecc719d6c12a7b80767d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~KingRavi\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Casework)\">Solution 2 (Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the first equation, we can express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fb72dc915fc10ca40d06bacff1fe3ebb2746732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y = 9 - x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b194070404b69d2208696d37ca7b7504efb22f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = (9 - x^2)/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>The second equation can be rewritten as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9ffc56fdfc026f4bc7aa50ce70a0fdcabd0c73d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + |y| - 4 = \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>This gives us two scenarios to examine:\n</p><p>1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/0631c8826d8aa9268a802f9c3f5c6215e0c2e160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + |y| = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab316e1ecdc459b5739afce879c9037ba66a681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + |y| = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Case 1:\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5b838274080dbd7dbbc94aa81db20acaeb3683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + |(9 - x^2)/3| = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>First, consider the case when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b5b030f50c77e2490c826f0accff8bb5c41fa83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - x^2 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" />. Then, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/0209d536685b89821c9bfdea5bb43838efbb4fef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y| = (9 - x^2)/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce44403f07a0907723f129d864e41db74b32e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + (9 - x^2)/3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying by 3, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b35e91567025532014146587bcf5c9114528134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|x| + 9 - x^2 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc1f94f2be19c0d05e52fb48c7ce9d5e698140c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|x| - x^2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d7cf7624f017ebd4506f39a39ad037517d16cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 3|x| + 6 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>However, the discriminant of this quadratic is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/986d041feeefc8af81038168675b7de712aa805a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-3)^2 - 4 * 1 * 6 = 9 - 24 = -15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"261\" height=\"21\" />, which indicates there are no real solutions in this scenario.\n</p><p>Now, we can consider when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c84c316096a310a331f52d18ee48076cbef622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - x^2 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/454ae6f764286862641edd7dfb6a76b3381bd3c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y| = -(9 - x^2)/3 = (x^2 - 9)/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"247\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278621a6fa2608f83cb295333195c7d55a540a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + (x^2 - 9)/3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying by 3, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5a6ad622d922f14511f69ae6fd6c7c7eb37e1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|x| + x^2 - 9 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2af1e171fc27cce00c9c848c2a1216a6c12786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 3|x| - 24 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/334d2d07cbbbf84fbc5eaf1be1a5eac2ee461921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = |x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a6e404cd33c1be22e440cb57a34f945d5e989e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2 + 3u - 24 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />. When we calculate the discriminant, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8c20119314efca8da49a265420a36b3d8f0514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2 - 4 * 1 * (-24) = 9 + 96 = 105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"265\" height=\"21\" />. So, the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd09182e702ac82b81d7a3bf4567a66212df8687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = (-3 \\pm \\sqrt(105))/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"173\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>Both roots give positive values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, resulting in two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for each root (one positive and one negative).\n</p><p>Case 2: \\( |x| + |y| = 3 \\)\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffaef1bb7cfb39cd4afbced6852a3be6f09d9a42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| +  |(9 - x^2)/3| = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b5b030f50c77e2490c826f0accff8bb5c41fa83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - x^2 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/0209d536685b89821c9bfdea5bb43838efbb4fef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y| = (9 - x^2)/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" /> which is |<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c402f2872264e96bc14d2da0669930d871fada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x| + (9 - x^2)/3 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying by 3, we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091934ed83bebf4c467ffcf90c52ac2903ae8e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|x| + 9 - x^2 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce3d4a37290be50601f4c04c596fa00667deea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|x| = x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1ad1442a090594e16b03c7dd4b8ff921e455c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 3|x| = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd3388d0bb698e9eab6c16c818b16841a189bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x|(|x| - 3) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />, leading to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> (both giving corresponding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> values).\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c84c316096a310a331f52d18ee48076cbef622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - x^2 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d31049d3d34ebd1c252f3c59b8e28ecb5f231a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y| = (x^2 - 9)/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd61d472652fb9a022982bd382a53a453a06b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + (x^2 - 9)/3 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>When we multiply through, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f20fa9662870aed89414996e0c65adc11bf2c84c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|x| + x^2 - 9 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cfa4ba44ec0dcc139a2a42a0bccdba956e1faa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 3|x| - 18 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>The discriminant here is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e7657dbc190f936f358fcbf95bfe6c8d435f914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2 - 4 * 1 * (-18) = 9 + 72 = 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"256\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>This gives two more real roots for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/334d2d07cbbbf84fbc5eaf1be1a5eac2ee461921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = |x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now, \n</p><p>- Case 1 contributes 2 solutions\n</p><p>- Case 2 contributes 1 solution from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, and 2 solutions from the second sub-case\n</p><p>Thus, counting all solutions gives us a total of 5 unique ordered pairs, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c4efc7de2b7c8d6f24ecc719d6c12a7b80767d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~goofytaipan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/yASY-XL9vtI\">https://youtu.be/yASY-XL9vtI</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zq3UPu4nwsE?t=974\">https://youtu.be/zq3UPu4nwsE?t=974</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5SVmxNrZUbY\">https://youtu.be/5SVmxNrZUbY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A\">2021 Fall AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AM